WEBVTT

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.400
<b>Reservations Open for Christmas Cake 
Cake Delivery (Frozen) Until 12/13</b>

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.440
This stuff goes over there!

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:06.400
Hurry!

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.240
<b>Reservations Open for Christmas Cake 
Cake Delivery (Frozen) Until 12/13</b>

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.410
I'm done sorting here!

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:11.560
Then, help them over there!

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:12.270
Right!

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:17.410
<b>Kenzaki Transport</b>

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:17.090
<i>The year's coming to a close, 
and it's the Christmas season.</i>

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.940
<i>But it's also the season
for making money at work.</i>

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:26.250
<b> This Way Up</b>

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.090
<b> This Way Up</b>

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.160
Are you okay?

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:31.710
S-Sorry.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:36.890
<b> This Way Up</b>

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.820
This sticker means the package 
should be upright at all times.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:36.880
Be careful.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:38.840
Oh, really?

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:43.750
If you don't know what something means, ask.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:44.850
S-Sure!

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:50.000
They're starting to sound like veterans.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:53.980
Until just recently, they were green.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:55.110
You're right.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:38.840
<b>Twenty-sixth Haunting 
Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</b>

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:46.550
<i>Christmas, huh?</i>

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:49.850
<i>Guess it's almost the end of the year, huh?</i>

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:55.720
Sorry!

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:58.020
Yumi!

00:02:58.410 --> 00:02:59.720
Yushi-kun?

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:01.850
It's been forever!

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.640
Hi, Yushi.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.520
You look very well.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:06.750
George, too?

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.760
Hey, there...

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:12.610
Wait, why are you two dressed like that?

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:15.670
We're off to a Christmas party!

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.600
George and I were chosen to be the Santas.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:22.020
Well? Do I look good?

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.660
Oh, very cute, Yumi.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.550
Thank you, George.

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:32.770
So, then, see you later, Yushi-kun!

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:34.950
George, let's go!

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.360
Okay, Yumi.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.710
Bye, Yushi.

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:39.390
B-Bye!

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:48.550
Yumi's so friendly with
George and his circle now.

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:50.730
Maybe too friendly.

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:55.240
Thank you!

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:07.970
<i>Takenaka?</i>

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:10.570
<i>What is he doing here?</i>

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:14.840
Hey, Takenaka!

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.090
Once you're done there, come in here!

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.270
Stop slacking!

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:19.940
O-Okay.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:20.810
Here.

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:25.220
After you drink it, back to work.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:26.070
Yes, sir.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:33.580
<i>It was up to them, alone, to quit being thugs.</i>

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:38.150
<i>Maybe it was all fated, from the start.</i>

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.530
<i>Everyone is working hard.</i>

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:55.160
<i>I need to work hard, too...</i>

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.560
To qualify as a government employee!

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:02.220
Master, I would prefer if you said, "As a mage."

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:03.850
Ain't happening.

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:06.480
Who are you talking to, Yu-kun?

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:14.290
Eri-chan?

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:15.360
What are you doing here?

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:17.520
That's my line.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.500
I was just out shopping for a bit.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.800
Why did I have to run into you?

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:25.600
You won't come home for New 
Year's or Christmas, right?

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:27.210
What are you thinking?

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:28.670
Uh, well...

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:32.680
As you can see, work keeps me really busy.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:37.390
I told your mom and dad I'd be 
home for spring break, but...

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:38.810
Was that a problem?

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:41.580
I-It isn't a problem, but...

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:43.890
Jeez, forget it!

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:49.310
What was that?

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:50.280
Who can say?

00:05:56.470 --> 00:06:00.360
<i>And time passed... And New Year's Eve arrived.</i>

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:02.190
Go!

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:05.170
Way to go, Hase-kun.

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:06.570
Have experience with this?

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:08.580
No... It's my first time.

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:11.020
You're looking pretty good, though.

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:13.220
But what about me?

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:16.900
It's the same as... a golf swing!

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:19.770
Damn it, you bourgeois swine!

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.160
It's a talent.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:22.950
I'll crush you!

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:24.350
Bring it!

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:26.660
They're a good pair...

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:44.670
Hot pot is the best part of winter!

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.630
It's so good!

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:48.340
It warms you up...

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:50.760
Right down to your bones.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.570
Here, say, "Ahhh."

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:53.630
Ahhh...

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:56.270
This is really good!

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:58.100
Especially, the meat.

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:05.440
I can feel warmth spreading 
throughout my entire body.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:08.760
Tonight, we will drink good sake again, as well.

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:13.030
Ruriko-san, more beer!

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.530
Are there any bad kids here?

00:07:19.030 --> 00:07:21.380
Are there any bad kids here?

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.380
The oni?!

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:22.420
They're namahage oni!

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:23.640
Those are real.

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:25.580
Huh? Seriously?!

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:28.170
Are there any bad kids here?

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:30.940
Oh, no... They're seriously real!

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:32.000
Scary.

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:36.540
Hot pot... Japanese food.

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:38.440
Let me have some!

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:42.510
Are you the bad kid?!

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:55.810
Cheers!

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:13.050
Happy New Year!

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:15.320
Welcome to the new year!

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:18.720
They'll keep partying a while longer, yeah?

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:20.430
It's New Year's, after all.

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:22.970
We have to put Kuri to bed.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:33.330
There isn't enough snow to play in, huh?

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:37.970
If it snows again, there might be enough.

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:41.120
There's snow.

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:46.950
Next to the waterfall, the landlord 
opened a hole to the tundra.

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:49.540
After New Year's, everyone will go play there!

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:51.440
The tundra?

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:09.890
Wow...

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:11.320
It's pure-white.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:19.330
This is fun!

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:26.270
Go, Kuri...

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:28.080
Show Mommy who's boss!

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:31.050
I'll get you!

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:34.600
Wait, wait!

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:36.380
What is that?

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:37.570
What's going on?

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:41.500
Snow huts?

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:43.390
Who made them?

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:47.320
Are these the snow huts of time?

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.590
Of time?

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:49.810
What are they?

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:54.350
Mysterious snow huts, appearing
between New Year's Eve

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:57.490
and dawn of the year's first day.

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:02.070
They say that if you enter, 
you can see the past and future.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:06.790
A strong wish lets one who enters 
to see related pasts and futures.

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:08.660
Pasts and futures?

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:10.140
Indeed...

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:15.100
Perhaps your powerful spiritual 
energy attracted them to us.

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:17.090
So impressive!

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:20.400
Master, you jerk!

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:24.600
Snow huts of time... Sounds fun.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.690
I mean, don't we have to take a look?

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:33.430
What is this?

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:34.940
How do you like it?

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:36.920
Pretty classy, huh?

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:38.820
Y-Yeah...

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:41.250
Hey, isn't that you?

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:55.180
That was the first time I came 
to the Yokai Apartments!

00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:58.850
Oh, yeah. I get food, too.

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:01.010
I wonder how it is.

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:04.810
This way, Yushi-kun.

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:06.740
Coming!

00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:11.420
I knew it!

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:13.290
We really are in the past!

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:14.670
Wow!

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:18.150
Kuri? Huh?

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:21.300
Two... Kuris?

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:23.410
I see.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.540
Then, you're the past Kuri?

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:31.860
We're back.

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:36.540
When someone from the past 
realizes you are from the future,

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:39.320
you will be sent back!

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:41.120
Be careful!

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:44.050
Hey, Kuri!

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:54.400
Is that Oda Nobunaga-san?!

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:55.470
What?

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:57.570
Someone else from the future?

00:11:57.840 --> 00:11:59.870
I'm sick of it...

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:03.450
All these people just keep coming!

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:05.580
Leave!

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:08.920
Please... Leave!

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:14.290
What was that?

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:15.830
Enough with the past...

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:17.450
Let's go see the future!

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:18.590
The future?

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:21.160
Yeah! My future!

00:12:21.410 --> 00:12:23.450
Show me my future...

00:12:23.450 --> 00:12:26.050
The one in which I work for the government!

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:31.940
Looks like we're in Las Vegas.

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:33.320
Las Vegas?

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:35.300
What am I doing here?

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:37.520
Some kind of departmental trip?

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:47.870
Th-That's... my future self?

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:05.060
What's happened to my future self?

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:07.340
Inaba... Look.

00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:12.050
Yushi, lend me some chips!

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:15.980
Cut it out, Furuhonya-san.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:17.650
Come on...

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:20.230
Aren't we traveling the world together?

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:23.140
Now, I'm regretting that a little, though.

00:13:23.140 --> 00:13:26.830
Don't say that, Yushi-sama!

00:13:26.830 --> 00:13:28.760
Wh-Why?

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:30.520
What about my dream of government work?

00:13:30.520 --> 00:13:32.360
It's a great future...

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:34.420
Traveling the world.

00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:36.150
No!

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:40.100
What are you doing here?

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:42.420
Well, whatever.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:44.370
Lend me some cash!

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:51.490
Furuhonya-san doesn't change, huh?

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:55.120
No... That has to be some kind of mistake.

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:58.930
All right! My turn next!

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:01.940
Follow me, future traveler!

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:02.870
Shut up!

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:07.710
Today, at noon, you have lunch with the 
Federation of Economic Organizations.

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:11.160
And then, at 2:00, a presentation from R&D.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:16.870
At 17:30, you leave Narita on your trip 
to examine the European markets.

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:19.750
Got it. Thanks.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:21.660
That's the future you?

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:22.800
Way to go, me.

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:24.180
That's kind of upsetting!

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:29.090
Also, sir, I'd like to confirm
the details of the recent transaction.

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:28.520
Wait, this voice... Tashiro?

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:30.810
I'll leave it to you.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:34.460
Your information is never wrong.

00:14:34.460 --> 00:14:35.900
Understood.

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:38.300
Leave everything to me.

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:43.350
It appears Hase-sama has gotten 
the future he wanted.

00:14:43.350 --> 00:14:45.160
Splendid.

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:46.320
Of course.

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:48.350
I can't accept this!

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.970
<i>Why only Hase?</i>

00:14:54.970 --> 00:14:57.150
<i>I should have an ideal future, too!</i>

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:02.170
<b>Popular Novelist-Adventurer! 
Yushi Inaba: Autograph Session</b>

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:03.450
I'm looking forward to your 
next book, Inaba-sensei!

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:05.120
Thank you.

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:08.770
Inaba-sensei! Die with me!

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:14.740
Glad it was a hardcover...

00:15:15.020 --> 00:15:16.940
This isn't right, either!

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:20.890
We're back at the Yokai Apartments?

00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:27.630
Hmm, this isn't the future.
It is a parallel world.

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:29.950
Is that even possible?

00:15:37.090 --> 00:15:38.100
Kuri!

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:43.530
K-Kuri!

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:46.760
What's going on?

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:50.140
This is a dimensional rift.

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:51.390
A dimensional rift?

00:15:51.390 --> 00:15:54.520
We have been caught in the flow of time!

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:58.050
At this rate, we shall never be 
able to return to our world.

00:15:58.220 --> 00:15:59.210
What?

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:02.640
Hase... Kuri!

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:05.730
<i>I... I can't let it end here!</i>

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:07.720
<i>We have a future!</i>

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:09.810
<i>I just saw it!</i>

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:13.410
<i>We're going back to the apartment.</i>

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:15.330
<i>I'm going to save Hase and Kuri!</i>

00:16:15.590 --> 00:16:18.590
<i>That is what I should do now.</i>

00:16:18.590 --> 00:16:23.080
Master, there should be an 
escape path, somewhere,

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:25.000
if you can only find it.

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:26.920
<i>Somewhere, there's a path.</i>

00:16:27.970 --> 00:16:28.870
The Sun,

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:30.080
Ignis Fatuus!

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:35.280
Light our path!

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:40.880
It didn't work?

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:42.760
N-No!

00:16:54.770 --> 00:16:56.620
Inaba, over there!

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:57.660
Got it!

00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:59.910
The Chariot, Hippogriff!

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:09.440
The proud Hippogriff is
allowing humans to ride it?

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:11.460
Way to go, master!

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:16.030
<i>We're going back to where everyone is...</i>

00:17:16.030 --> 00:17:18.560
<i>To the Yokai Apartments!</i>

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:20.240
Please, Hippogriff!

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:22.740
Take us back to our world!

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:26.300
Everyone...

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:36.190
Wh-Where are we?

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:40.430
We're saved!

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:43.270
Yushi-kun...

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:45.010
Ryu-san!

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:46.230
Yushi-kun!

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:49.620
Everyone, we found them!

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:51.050
I'm so glad...

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:52.620
Everyone appears to be safe.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:56.040
Jeez, don't start the new
year by causing trouble.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:59.040
You were all... looking for us?

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:05.060
I feel alive again!

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:09.830
The snow huts of time, hmm?

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:13.140
That's a rare thing you found!

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:16.580
You protected Hase-kun and 
Kuri. And you returned.

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:18.760
Well done, Yushi-kun.

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.500
Not at all.

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:23.150
But that experience was valuable.

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:27.460
What you saw wasn't
the real future, specifically.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:29.330
It was a possible future.

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:31.120
A possible future?

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:32.080
Yes.

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:34.600
A future that might come to be.

00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:36.950
None of them is the real future.

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:40.510
Your choices make your future.

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:44.330
That's why you need to make 
choices you won't regret.

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:48.310
Because it's your future, and yours alone.

00:18:48.430 --> 00:18:50.500
Your future, alone.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:52.830
I see...

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:56.020
We have infinite futures.

00:18:56.020 --> 00:18:58.140
Infinite possibilities!

00:18:58.310 --> 00:18:59.660
That's right.

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:01.460
I'd hope so...

00:19:01.460 --> 00:19:04.320
That wasn't the future I want.

00:19:04.610 --> 00:19:08.320
You want even more? That's just like you.

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:09.250
I guess so.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:13.500
Also, I can't imagine a future without you.

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:15.120
R-Right...

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:17.080
Thanks.

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:20.530
Well? What future did you see, Yushi?

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:21.810
Right, right.

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:23.920
I'm so curious!

00:19:23.920 --> 00:19:26.250
Tell us... Come on.

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:27.600
Well,

00:19:28.010 --> 00:19:31.430
I was in the snow hut, relaxing with everyone!

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:35.420
The sun's risen.

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:40.570
It's so pretty...

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:41.690
Really.

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:44.320
It's so pretty!

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:48.360
M-Mariko-san, cover yourself!

00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:51.160
I forgot my towel!

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:55.780
Okay! Let's start the new year off right!

00:19:55.780 --> 00:19:57.020
Ready?

00:19:57.020 --> 00:19:58.780
Cheers!

00:19:59.390 --> 00:20:01.210
Yes!

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:05.130
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

00:20:09.210 --> 00:20:12.490
<i>Partying in the new year, 
alongside those I love.</i>

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:15.130
<i>This is the future I choose.</i>

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:18.310
This year, let's take it easy.

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:19.390
Yeah!

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:26.710
Morning!

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:29.540
How was your New Year's, Inaba?

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:31.490
It was great!

00:20:32.390 --> 00:20:34.320
Wow, I'm really curious!

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:36.430
Oh, what happened?

00:20:36.430 --> 00:20:37.820
What happened?

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:39.740
I'm so excited... I'm so excited...

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:45.260
Looks like you're having fun, Inaba.

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:46.670
I guess I am.

00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:56.230
<i>I've made many choices,</i>

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:59.330
<i>and seen many different karmas.</i>

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:03.280
<i>What other encounters will I have?</i>

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:07.270
<i>What future awaits me?</i>

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:10.990
<i>When I think about it,</i>

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:13.800
<i>I get really excited.</i>

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:16.080
<i>That's right.</i>

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>Just like the first day I came 
to the Yokai Apartments.</i>

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:27.190
It's always so lively here, chirp.

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:29.670
And it will always stay that way, chirp!

00:21:29.670 --> 00:21:33.130
<i>That's the elegant Yokai
Apartment life, chirp!</i>

00:21:34.690 --> 00:21:36.400
Chirp! Chirp! Chirp!

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:38.140
Chirpity-chirp! Chirp!
